[
    {
        "text": "You may Wonder what gives NFTs their value. Why would someone be willing to pay money for a digital picture when you can just save the file from the Internet? The value of an NFT works in a similar way to a piece of art. If you can prove that you own an original Picasso painting, then you can sell it for a lot of money or brag about your ownership. Anyone can make a copy of a Picasso painting because it's in the public domain, and if it's on display, anyone can look at it. But copies and viewing access do not diminish the value of a Picasso. Perhaps they even enhance it. The same goes for collectibles like rare baseball cards or collectible game cards. Proof of ownership and the rights that go along with that ownership are what NFTs represent.",
        "start": 480,
        "end": 41900,
        "confidence": 0.9899781,
